steps.reply:
The recursive SHC run diverged wildly (feedback instability), so I'll instead forecast each future visit independently from the parcel's own history using seasonal analogs (same time-of-year across the 4 observed years), which fits this stationary series.

```bash
python3 - <<'PY'
import csv, json, datetime
from collections import defaultdict
rows=list(csv.DictReader(open("data.csv")))
hist=defaultdict(list)  # band -> [(date, value)]
for r in rows:
    hist[r["band"]].append((datetime.date.fromisoformat(r["date"]), float(r["y"])))
def doy(d, y): return (d-datetime.date(y,1,1)).days
pred={}
for v in csv.DictReader(open("visits_to_predict.csv")):
    d=datetime.date.fromisoformat(v["date"])
    pred[v["period_id"]]={}
    for b,series in hist.items():
        # candidates: same day-of-year +/- window in each prior year, weight by proximity
        cands=[]
        for hd,val in series:
            if hd>=d: continue
            for yr in range(2020,2025):
                try: target=datetime.date(yr,d.month,d.day)
                except ValueError: target=None
                if target:
                    delta=abs((hd-target).days)
                    if delta<=16: cands.append((delta,val,hd.year))
        if not cands:
            pred[v["period_id"]][b]=round(series[-1][1],4); continue
        num=sum(val*(17-dl) for dl,val,yr in cands)
        den=sum(17-dl for dl,val,yr in cands)
        pred[v["period_id"]][b]=round(num/den,4)
json.dump({"prediction":pred,"rationale":"Recursive application of the SHC one-step forecast diverged (feedback instability), so each future visit was forecast independently from the parcel's own 117-visit history (2020-09 to 2024-09) using seasonal analog matching: for each target date, historical observations within +/-16 days of the same calendar day in prior years were weighted-averaged (closer dates weighted higher) per band (VH, VV, VV-VH). The series is stationary (VH ~ -15, VV ~ -8.5, VV-VH ~ 6), so this yields plausible in-range forecasts for P118-P144."}, open("answer.json","w"), indent=1)
print(json.dumps(pred,indent=1))
PY
